.el .ds Aq '
.TH nut-completion 1  "nut-cli 0.1.0" nut
.SH NAME
nut\-completion \- Install, inspect, or remove shell completion
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBnut completion\fR [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-ascii\fR] [\fB\-j\fR|\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-c\fR|\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Install, inspect, or remove shell completion
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR [default: auto]
Color output policy
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-ascii\fR
Use ASCII symbols and bars
.TP
\fB\-j\fR, \fB\-\-json\fR
Emit machine\-readable JSON where supported
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Include additional diagnostic detail
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Read host settings from this file
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
nut\-completion\-install(1)
Install an adapter and verify registration in an isolated real shell
.TP
nut\-completion\-status(1)
Inspect installed adapters and probe their registration
.TP
nut\-completion\-uninstall(1)
Remove adapters whose bytes still match the recorded manifest
.TP
nut\-completion\-zsh(1)
Print the zsh adapter for manual installation
.TP
nut\-completion\-bash(1)
Print the bash adapter for manual installation
